## Current desk update

The authenticated [course challenge page](https://hq.mega.dev/challenges/what-it-shows)
now publishes an engineering update headed **#4471 · closed 05 oct**.
That is the source's stated closure date; this page was reviewed later. The original
export was dated 2026-10-04 and did not contain this update.

| Problem | Desk update, verbatim | GitHub disposition |
| --- | --- | --- |
| parser | FIXED — fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales | [Issue #1](https://github.com/tmoasz/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1): closed, completed |
| hint | WON'T FIX — booking-v3 form retired | [Issue #2](https://github.com/tmoasz/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2): closed, not planned |

These outcomes must not be collapsed into “both fixed”. The parser has a reported fix;
the hint is no longer planned because the affected form was retired. The issue closure
comments identify the desk update as the authority. This repository does not contain the
production patch or claim to have independently retested it.

## Evidence and historical counts

The [signed triage decision](/kb/decisions/0002-evidence-based-triage/) preserves the
computed report counts, exact memberships, intake disagreements, source timestamps,
and five desk-note caveats. Those historical counts do not change when issues close.
The initial course submission accepted the two tickets; acceptance of that step was not
acceptance of the whole challenge.

The five exceptional bodies remain an evidence limitation: four report one-day symptoms,
and one describes an invite preceding booking. The desk's closure update does not
supply individual reproductions for them. Do not invent a timezone fix or erase their
quotations to make the history look simpler.

## Maintaining this knowledge

The old exported incident and decision 0001 remain historical evidence. Decision 0002
replaces subject-only triage without rewriting the accepted old decision. This separate
resolution page records the later desk state instead of silently changing that accepted
analysis. For subsequent status changes, verify the live desk source and issue state,
then add a dated update with its provenance.

